---User metadata of the request.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistUserMetadata
---@field timeZone? string Optional. IANA time zone, e.g. Europe/Budapest.
---@field preferredLanguageCode? string Optional. Preferred language to be used for answering if language detection fails. Also used as the language of error messages created by actions, regardless of language detection results.

---Discovery Engine Assistant resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistant
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was most recently updated.
---@field defaultWebGroundingToggleOff? boolean Optional. This field controls the default web grounding toggle for end users if `web_grounding_type` is set to `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`. By default, this field is set to false. If `web_grounding_type` is `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`, end users will have web grounding enabled by default on UI. If true, grounding toggle will be disabled by default on UI. End users can still enable web grounding in the UI if web grounding is enabled.
---@field displayName? string Required. The assistant display name. It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field name? string Immutable. Resource name of the assistant. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/assistants/{assistant}` It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field customerPolicy? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicy Optional. Customer policy for the assistant.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was created.
---@field webGroundingType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantWebGroundingTypeEnum Optional. The type of web grounding to use.
---@field generationConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantGenerationConfig Optional. Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
---@field description? string Optional. Description for additional information. Expected to be shown on the configuration UI, not to the users of the assistant.
---@field enabledTools? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantToolListMap Optional. The enabled tools on this assistant. The keys are data connector resource names, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector`. The values are the tools that the admin enabled on that connector. Admins can selectively enable tools on any of the connectors that they created in the project. For example: ``` { "projects/my-project/locations/global/collections/jira1/dataConnector": { "toolInfo": [ { "toolName": "create_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Create Jira issue" }, { "toolName": "update_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Update Jira issue" } ] } } ```

---Multi-modal content.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContent
---@field executableCode? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentExecutableCode Code generated by the model that is meant to be executed.
---@field thought? boolean Optional. Indicates if the part is thought from the model.
---@field inlineData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentBlob Inline binary data.
---@field role? string The producer of the content. Can be "model" or "user".
---@field text? string Inline text.
---@field file? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentFile A file, e.g., an audio summary.
---@field codeExecutionResult? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentCodeExecutionResult Result of executing an ExecutableCode.

---Inline blob.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentBlob
---@field data? string Required. Raw bytes.
---@field mimeType? string Required. The media type (MIME type) of the generated data.

---Result of executing ExecutableCode.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentCodeExecutionResult
---@field outcome? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentCodeExecutionResultOutcomeEnum|string Required. Outcome of the code execution.
---@field output? string Optional. Contains stdout when code execution is successful, stderr or other description otherwise.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentCodeExecutionResultOutcomeEnum "OUTCOME_UNSPECIFIED"|"OUTCOME_OK"|"OUTCOME_FAILED"|"OUTCOME_DEADLINE_EXCEEDED"

---Code generated by the model that is meant to be executed by the model.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentExecutableCode
---@field code? string Required. The code content. Currently only supports Python.

---A file, e.g., an audio summary.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantContentFile
---@field fileId? string Required. The file ID.
---@field mimeType? string Required. The media type (MIME type) of the file.

---Customer-defined policy for the assistant.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicy
---@field modelArmorConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfig Optional. Model Armor configuration to be used for sanitizing user prompts and assistant responses.
---@field bannedPhrases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseList Optional. List of banned phrases.
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDataProtectionPolicy Optional. Data protection policy to be used for sanitizing file uploads.

---Definition of a customer-defined banned phrase. A banned phrase is not allowed to appear in the user query or the LLM response, or else the answer will be refused.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhrase
---@field phrase? string Required. The raw string content to be banned.
---@field matchType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseMatchTypeEnum|string Optional. Match type for the banned phrase.
---@field ignoreDiacritics? boolean Optional. If true, diacritical marks (e.g., accents, umlauts) are ignored when matching banned phrases. For example, "cafe" would match "café".

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhrase[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseMatchTypeEnum "BANNED_PHRASE_MATCH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SIMPLE_STRING_MATCH"|"WORD_BOUNDARY_STRING_MATCH"

---Configuration for customer defined Model Armor templates to be used for sanitizing user prompts and assistant responses.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfig
---@field responseTemplate? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template for sanitizing assistant responses. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template_id}` If not specified, no sanitization will be applied to the assistant response.
---@field userPromptTemplate? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template for sanitizing user prompts. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template_id}` If not specified, no sanitization will be applied to the user prompt.
---@field failureMode? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfigFailureModeEnum|string Optional. Defines the failure mode for Model Armor sanitization.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfigFailureModeEnum "FAILURE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FAIL_OPEN"|"FAIL_CLOSED"

---Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantGenerationConfig
---@field defaultLanguage? string The default language to use for the generation of the assistant response. Use an ISO 639-1 language code such as `en`. If not specified, the language will be automatically detected.
---@field systemInstruction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantGenerationConfigSystemInstruction System instruction, also known as the prompt preamble for LLM calls. See also https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/prompts/system-instructions
---@field defaultModelId? string Optional. The default model to use for assistant.
---@field allowedModelIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. The list of models that are allowed to be used for assistant.

---System instruction, also known as the prompt preamble for LLM calls.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAssistantGenerationConfigSystemInstruction
---@field additionalSystemInstruction? string Optional. Additional system instruction that will be added to the default system instruction.

