---@field dataIngestionSource? string The data ingestion source of the Document. Allowed values are: * `batch`: Data ingested via Batch API, e.g., ImportDocuments. * `streaming` Data ingested via Streaming API, e.g., FHIR streaming.
---@field lastRefreshedTime? string The timestamp of the last time the Document was last indexed.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadata[]

---The value of the matcher that was used to match the Document.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataMatcherValue
---@field uri? string If match by URI, the URI of the Document.
---@field fhirResource? string Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}/fhirStores/{fhir_store}/fhir/{resource_type}/{fhir_resource_id}

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INDEXED"|"NOT_IN_TARGET_SITE"|"NOT_IN_INDEX"

---The inline source for the input config for BatchUpdateUserLicenses method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBatchUpdateUserLicensesRequestInlineSource
---@field userLicenses? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaUserLicenseList Required. A list of user licenses to update. Each user license must have a valid UserLicense.user_principal.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to update.

---Request message for SiteSearchEngineService.BatchVerifyTargetSites method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBatchVerifyTargetSitesRequest

---BigQuery source import data from.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigQuerySource
---@field dataSchema? string The schema to use when parsing the data from the source. Supported values for user event imports: * `user_event` (default): One UserEvent per row. Supported values for document imports: * `document` (default): One Document format per row. Each document must have a valid Document.id and one of Document.json_data or Document.struct_data. * `custom`: One custom data per row in arbitrary format that conforms to the defined Schema of the data store. This can only be used by the GENERIC Data Store vertical.
---@field partitionDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleTypeDate BigQuery time partitioned table's _PARTITIONDATE in YYYY-MM-DD format.
---@field projectId? string The project ID or the project number that contains the BigQuery source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.
---@field datasetId? string Required. The BigQuery data set to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,024 characters.
---@field gcsStagingDir? string Intermediate Cloud Storage directory used for the import with a length limit of 2,000 characters. Can be specified if one wants to have the BigQuery export to a specific Cloud Storage directory.
---@field tableId? string Required. The BigQuery table to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,024 characters.

---The Bigtable Options object that contains information to support the import.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptions
---@field keyFieldName? string The field name used for saving row key value in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`.
---@field families? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyMap The mapping from family names to an object that contains column families level information for the given column family. If a family is not present in this map it will be ignored.

---The column of the Bigtable.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumn
---@field type? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnTypeEnum|string The type of values in this column family. The values are expected to be encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` function when the encoding value is set to `BINARY`.
---@field qualifier? string Required. Qualifier of the column. If it cannot be decoded with utf-8, use a base-64 encoded string instead.
---@field fieldName? string The field name to use for this column in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`. If not set, it is parsed from the qualifier bytes with best effort. However, due to different naming patterns, field name collisions could happen, where parsing behavior is undefined.
---@field encoding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnEncodingEnum|string The encoding mode of the values when the type is not `STRING`. Acceptable encoding values are: * `TEXT`: indicates values are alphanumeric text strings. * `BINARY`: indicates values are encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` family of functions. This can be overridden for a specific column by listing that column in `columns` and specifying an encoding for it.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"BINARY"

---The column family of the Bigtable.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamily
---@field type? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyTypeEnum|string The type of values in this column family. The values are expected to be encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` function when the encoding value is set to `BINARY`.
---@field fieldName? string The field name to use for this column family in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`. If not set, it is parsed from the family name with best effort. However, due to different naming patterns, field name collisions could happen, where parsing behavior is undefined.
---@field columns? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnList The list of objects that contains column level information for each column. If a column is not present in this list it will be ignored.
---@field encoding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyEncodingEnum|string The encoding mode of the values when the type is not STRING. Acceptable encoding values are: * `TEXT`: indicates values are alphanumeric text strings. * `BINARY`: indicates values are encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` family of functions. This can be overridden for a specific column by listing that column in `columns` and specifying an encoding for it.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"BINARY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamily }

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"INTEGER"|"VAR_INTEGER"|"BIG_NUMERIC"|"BOOLEAN"|"JSON"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumn[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"INTEGER"|"VAR_INTEGER"|"BIG_NUMERIC"|"BOOLEAN"|"JSON"

---The Cloud Bigtable source for importing data.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableSource
---@field tableId? string Required. The table ID of the Cloud Bigtable that needs to be imported.
---@field projectId? string The project ID that contains the Bigtable source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.
---@field instanceId? string Required. The instance ID of the Cloud Bigtable that needs to be imported.
---@field bigtableOptions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaBigtableOptions Required. Bigtable options that contains information needed when parsing data into typed structures. For example, column type annotations.

---Response message for the GroundedGenerationService.CheckGrounding method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponse
---@field citedChunks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaFactChunkList List of facts cited across all claims in the answer candidate. These are derived from the facts supplied in the request.
---@field claims? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseClaimList Claim texts and citation info across all claims in the answer candidate.
---@field supportScore? number The support score for the input answer candidate. Higher the score, higher is the fraction of claims that are supported by the provided facts. This is always set when a response is returned.
---@field citedFacts? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunkList List of facts cited across all claims in the answer candidate. These are derived from the facts supplied in the request.

---Fact chunk for grounding check.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunk
---@field chunkText? string Text content of the fact chunk. Can be at most 10K characters long.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunkList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunk[]

---Text and citation info for a claim in the answer candidate.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseClaim
---@field score? number Confidence score for the claim in the answer candidate, in the range of [0, 1]. This is set only when `CheckGroundingRequest.grounding_spec.enable_claim_level_score` is true.
---@field startPos? number Position indicating the start of the claim in the answer candidate, measured in bytes. Note that this is not measured in characters and, therefore, must be rendered in the user interface keeping in mind that some characters may take more than one byte. For example, if the claim text contains non-ASCII characters, the start and end positions vary when measured in characters (programming-language-dependent) and when measured in bytes (programming-language-independent).
---@field citationIndices? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.IntegerList A list of indices (into 'cited_chunks') specifying the citations associated with the claim. For instance [1,3,4] means that cited_chunks[1], cited_chunks[3], cited_chunks[4] are the facts cited supporting for the claim. A citation to a fact indicates that the claim is supported by the fact.
---@field claimText? string Text for the claim in the answer candidate. Always provided regardless of whether citations or anti-citations are found.
---@field groundingCheckRequired? boolean Indicates that this claim required grounding check. When the system decided this claim doesn't require attribution/grounding check, this field will be set to false. In that case, no grounding check was done for the claim and therefore citation_indices should not be returned.
---@field endPos? number Position indicating the end of the claim in the answer candidate, exclusive, in bytes. Note that this is not measured in characters and, therefore, must be rendered as such. For example, if the claim text contains non-ASCII characters, the start and end positions vary when measured in characters (programming-language-dependent) and when measured in bytes (programming-language-independent).

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseClaimList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingResponseClaim[]

---Specification for the grounding check.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCheckGroundingSpec
---@field enableClaimLevelScore? boolean The control flag that enables claim-level grounding score in the response.
---@field citationThreshold? number The threshold (in [0,1]) used for determining whether a fact must be cited for a claim in the answer candidate. Choosing a higher threshold will lead to fewer but very strong citations, while choosing a lower threshold may lead to more but somewhat weaker citations. If unset, the threshold will default to 0.6.

---Chunk captures all raw metadata information of items to be recommended or searched in the chunk mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunk
---@field id? string Unique chunk ID of the current chunk.
---@field chunkMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkChunkMetadata Output only. Metadata of the current chunk.
---@field annotationContents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Output only. Annotation contents if the current chunk contains annotations.
---@field relevanceScore? number Output only. Represents the relevance score based on similarity. Higher score indicates higher chunk relevance. The score is in range [-1.0, 1.0]. Only populated on SearchResponse.
---@field dataUrls? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Output only. Image Data URLs if the current chunk contains images. Data URLs are composed of four parts: a prefix (data:), a MIME type indicating the type of data, an optional base64 token if non-textual, and the data itself: data:,
---@field content? string Content is a string from a document (parsed content).
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field pageSpan? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkPageSpan Page span of the chunk.
---@field annotationMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkAnnotationMetadataList Output only. The annotation metadata includes structured content in the current chunk.
---@field documentMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkDocumentMetadata Metadata of the document from the current chunk.
---@field name? string The full resource name of the chunk. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}/chunks/{chunk_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---The annotation metadata includes structured content in the current chunk.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkAnnotationMetadata
---@field imageId? string Output only. Image id is provided if the structured content is based on an image.
---@field structuredContent? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkStructuredContent Output only. The structured content information.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkAnnotationMetadataList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkAnnotationMetadata[]

---Metadata of the current chunk. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkChunkMetadata
---@field nextChunks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkList The next chunks of the current chunk. The number is controlled by SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.ChunkSpec.num_next_chunks. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.
---@field previousChunks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkList The previous chunks of the current chunk. The number is controlled by SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.ChunkSpec.num_previous_chunks. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.

---Document metadata contains the information of the document of the current chunk.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkDocumentMetadata
---@field title? string Title of the document.
---@field mimeType? string The mime type of the document. https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml.
---@field structData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.DocumentMap Data representation. The structured JSON data for the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field uri? string Uri of the document.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunk[]

---Page span of the chunk.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkPageSpan
---@field pageStart? number The start page of the chunk.
---@field pageEnd? number The end page of the chunk.

---The structured content information.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkStructuredContent
---@field structureType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkStructuredContentStructureTypeEnum Output only. The structure type of the structured content.
---@field content? string Output only. The content of the structured content.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunkStructuredContentStructureTypeEnum "STRUCTURE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SHAREHOLDER_STRUCTURE"|"SIGNATURE_STRUCTURE"|"CHECKBOX_STRUCTURE"

---Source attributions for content.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCitation
---@field license? string Output only. License of the attribution.
---@field title? string Output only. Title of the attribution.
---@field endIndex? number Output only. End index into the content.
---@field uri? string Output only. Url reference of the attribution.
---@field publicationDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleTypeDate Output only. Publication date of the attribution.
---@field startIndex? number Output only. Start index into the content.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCitationList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCitation[]

---A collection of source attributions for a piece of content.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCitationMetadata
---@field citations? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCitationList Output only. List of citations.

---Cloud SQL source import data from.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCloudSqlSource
---@field databaseId? string Required. The Cloud SQL database to copy the data from with a length limit of 256 characters.
---@field tableId? string Required. The Cloud SQL table to copy the data from with a length limit of 256 characters.
---@field instanceId? string Required. The Cloud SQL instance to copy the data from with a length limit of 256 characters.
---@field gcsStagingDir? string Intermediate Cloud Storage directory used for the import with a length limit of 2,000 characters. Can be specified if one wants to have the Cloud SQL export to a specific Cloud Storage directory. Ensure that the Cloud SQL service account has the necessary Cloud Storage Admin permissions to access the specified Cloud Storage directory.
---@field offload? boolean Option for serverless export. Enabling this option will incur additional cost. More info can be found [here](https://cloud.google.com/sql/pricing#serverless).
---@field projectId? string The project ID that contains the Cloud SQL source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.

---Configurations used to enable CMEK data encryption with Cloud KMS keys.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfig
---@field isDefault? boolean Output only. The default CmekConfig for the Customer.
---@field kmsKeyVersion? string Output only. KMS key version resource name which will be used to encrypt resources `/cryptoKeyVersions/{keyVersion}`.
---@field name? string Required. The name of the CmekConfig of the form `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/cmekConfig` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/cmekConfigs/{cmek_config}`.
---@field lastRotationTimestampMicros? string Output only. The timestamp of the last key rotation.
---@field kmsKey? string Required. KMS key resource name which will be used to encrypt resources `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/keyRings/{keyRing}/cryptoKeys/{keyId}`.
---@field singleRegionKeys? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSingleRegionKeyList Optional. Single-regional CMEKs that are required for some VAIS features.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfigStateEnum|string Output only. The states of the CmekConfig.
---@field notebooklmState? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfigNotebooklmStateEnum|string Output only. Whether the NotebookLM Corpus is ready to be used.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfigList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfig[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfigNotebooklmStateEnum "NOTEBOOK_LM_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NOTEBOOK_LM_NOT_READY"|"NOTEBOOK_LM_READY"|"NOTEBOOK_LM_NOT_ENABLED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfigStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CREATING"|"ACTIVE"|"KEY_ISSUE"|"DELETING"|"DELETE_FAILED"|"UNUSABLE"|"ACTIVE_ROTATING"|"DELETED"|"EXPIRED"

---Response message for CompletionService.CompleteQuery method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompleteQueryResponse
---@field querySuggestions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestionList Results of the matched query suggestions. The result list is ordered and the first result is a top suggestion.
---@field tailMatchTriggered? boolean True if the returned suggestions are all tail suggestions. For tail matching to be triggered, include_tail_suggestions in the request must be true and there must be no suggestions that match the full query.

---Suggestions as search queries.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestion
---@field suggestion? string The suggestion for the query.
---@field completableFieldPaths? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList The unique document field paths that serve as the source of this suggestion if it was generated from completable fields. This field is only populated for the document-completable model.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestion[]

---Detailed completion information including completion attribution token and clicked completion info.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompletionInfo
---@field selectedSuggestion? string Optional. End user selected CompleteQueryResponse.QuerySuggestion.suggestion.
---@field selectedPosition? number End user selected CompleteQueryResponse.QuerySuggestion.suggestion position, starting from 0.

---Autocomplete suggestions that are imported from Customer.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompletionSuggestion
---@field alternativePhrases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Alternative matching phrases for this suggestion.
---@field globalScore? number Global score of this suggestion. Control how this suggestion would be scored / ranked.
---@field groupScore? number The score of this suggestion within its group.
---@field frequency? string Frequency of this suggestion. Will be used to rank suggestions when score is not available.
---@field languageCode? string BCP-47 language code of this suggestion.
---@field suggestion? string Required. The suggestion text.
---@field groupId? string If two suggestions have the same groupId, they will not be returned together. Instead the one ranked higher will be returned. This can be used to deduplicate semantically identical suggestions.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompletionSuggestionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCompletionSuggestion[]

---Defines circumstances to be checked before allowing a behavior
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCondition
---@field queryRegex? string Optional. Query regex to match the whole search query. Cannot be set when Condition.query_terms is set. Only supported for Basic Site Search promotion serving controls.
---@field activeTimeRange? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionTimeRangeList Range of time(s) specifying when condition is active. Maximum of 10 time ranges.
---@field queryTerms? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionQueryTermList Search only A list of terms to match the query on. Cannot be set when Condition.query_regex is set. Maximum of 10 query terms.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCondition[]

---Matcher for search request query
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionQueryTerm
---@field fullMatch? boolean Whether the search query needs to exactly match the query term.
---@field value? string The specific query value to match against Must be lowercase, must be UTF-8. Can have at most 3 space separated terms if full_match is true. Cannot be an empty string. Maximum length of 5000 characters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionQueryTermList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionQueryTerm[]

---Used for time-dependent conditions.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionTimeRange
---@field endTime? string End of time range. Range is inclusive. Must be in the future.
---@field startTime? string Start of time range. Range is inclusive.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionTimeRangeList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionTimeRange[]

---Defines a conditioned behavior to employ during serving. Must be attached to a ServingConfig to be considered at serving time. Permitted actions dependent on `SolutionType`.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControl
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field redirectAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlSolutionTypeEnum Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field conditions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`
---@field promoteAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field filterAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field useCases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.

---Adjusts order of products in returned list.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostAction
---@field filter? string Required. Specifies which products to apply the boost to. If no filter is provided all products will be boosted (No-op). Syntax documentation: https://cloud.google.com/retail/docs/filter-and-order Maximum length is 5000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boost? number Strength of the boost, which should be in [-1, 1]. Negative boost means demotion. Default is 0.0 (No-op).
---@field dataStore? string Required. Specifies which data store's documents can be boosted by this control. Full data store name e.g. projects/123/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/default_data_store
---@field interpolationBoostSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpec Optional. Complex specification for custom ranking based on customer defined attribute value.
---@field fixedBoost? number Optional. Strength of the boost, which should be in [-1, 1]. Negative boost means demotion. Default is 0.0 (No-op).

---Specification for custom ranking based on customer specified attribute value. It provides more controls for customized ranking than the simple (condition, boost) combination above.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpec
---@field attributeType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecAttributeTypeEnum|string Optional. The attribute type to be used to determine the boost amount. The attribute value can be derived from the field value of the specified field_name. In the case of numerical it is straightforward i.e. attribute_value = numerical_field_value. In the case of freshness however, attribute_value = (time.now() - datetime_field_value).
---@field controlPoints? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPointList Optional. The control points used to define the curve. The monotonic function (defined through the interpolation_type above) passes through the control points listed here.
---@field interpolationType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecInterpolationTypeEnum|string Optional. The interpolation type to be applied to connect the control points listed below.
---@field fieldName? string Optional. The name of the field whose value will be used to determine the boost amount.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecAttributeTypeEnum "ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NUMERICAL"|"FRESHNESS"

---The control points used to define the curve. The curve defined through these control points can only be monotonically increasing or decreasing(constant values are acceptable).
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPoint
---@field attributeValue? string Optional. Can be one of: 1. The numerical field value. 2. The duration spec for freshness: The value must be formatted as an XSD `dayTimeDuration` value (a restricted subset of an ISO 8601 duration value). The pattern for this is: `nDnM]`.
---@field boostAmount? number Optional. The value between -1 to 1 by which to boost the score if the attribute_value evaluates to the value specified above.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPointList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPoint[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecInterpolationTypeEnum "INTERPOLATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LINEAR"

---Specified which products may be included in results. Uses same filter as boost.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlFilterAction
---@field dataStore? string Required. Specifies which data store's documents can be filtered by this control. Full data store name e.g. projects/123/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/default_data_store
---@field filter? string Required. A filter to apply on the matching condition results. Required Syntax documentation: https://cloud.google.com/retail/docs/filter-and-order Maximum length is 5000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControlList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaControl[]

