---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDataStoreSolutionTypesItemEnum "SOLUTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_GENERATIVE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_AI_MODE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDataStoreSolutionTypesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDataStoreSolutionTypesItemEnum|string)[]

---The historical dedicated crawl rate timeseries data, used for monitoring. Dedicated crawl is used by Vertex AI to crawl the user's website when dedicate crawl is set.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDedicatedCrawlRateTimeSeries
---@field autoRefreshCrawlErrorRate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCrawlRateTimeSeries Vertex AI's error rate time series of auto-refresh dedicated crawl.
---@field userTriggeredCrawlErrorRate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCrawlRateTimeSeries Vertex AI's error rate time series of user triggered dedicated crawl.
---@field autoRefreshCrawlRate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCrawlRateTimeSeries Vertex AI's dedicated crawl rate time series of auto-refresh, which is the crawl rate of Google-CloudVertexBot when dedicate crawl is set, and the crawl rate is for best effort use cases like refreshing urls periodically.
---@field userTriggeredCrawlRate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCrawlRateTimeSeries Vertex AI's dedicated crawl rate time series of user triggered crawl, which is the crawl rate of Google-CloudVertexBot when dedicate crawl is set, and user triggered crawl rate is for deterministic use cases like crawling urls or sitemaps specified by users.

---Request message for SiteSearchEngineService.DisableAdvancedSiteSearch method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDisableAdvancedSiteSearchRequest

---Response message for LicenseConfigService.DistributeLicenseConfig method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDistributeLicenseConfigResponse
---@field licenseConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaLicenseConfig The updated or created LicenseConfig.

---Document captures all raw metadata information of items to be recommended or searched.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocument
---@field schemaId? string The identifier of the schema located in the same data store.
---@field content? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentContent The unstructured data linked to this document. Content can only be set and must be set if this document is under a `CONTENT_REQUIRED` data store.
---@field id? string Immutable. The identifier of the document. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field indexStatus? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentIndexStatus Output only. The index status of the document. * If document is indexed successfully, the index_time field is populated. * Otherwise, if document is not indexed due to errors, the error_samples field is populated. * Otherwise, if document's index is in progress, the pending_message field is populated.
---@field indexTime? string Output only. The time when the document was last indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours. If this field is not populated, it means the document has never been indexed.
---@field aclInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentAclInfo Access control information for the document.
---@field parentDocumentId? string The identifier of the parent document. Currently supports at most two level document hierarchy. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 63 characters.
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field name? string Immutable. The full resource name of the document. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field jsonData? string The JSON string representation of the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field structData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.DocumentMap The structured JSON data for the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.

---ACL Information of the Document.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentAclInfo
---@field readers? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentAclInfoAccessRestrictionList Readers of the document.

---AclRestriction to model complex inheritance restrictions. Example: Modeling a "Both Permit" inheritance, where to access a child document, user needs to have access to parent document. Document Hierarchy - Space_S --> Page_P. Readers: Space_S: group_1, user_1 Page_P: group_2, group_3, user_2 Space_S ACL Restriction - { "acl_info": { "readers": [ { "principals": [ { "group_id": "group_1" }, { "user_id": "user_1" } ] } ] } } Page_P ACL Restriction. { "acl_info": { "readers": [ { "principals": [ { "group_id": "group_2" }, { "group_id": "group_3" }, { "user_id": "user_2" } ], }, { "principals": [ { "group_id": "group_1" }, { "user_id": "user_1" } ], } ] } }
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentAclInfoAccessRestriction
---@field idpWide? boolean All users within the Identity Provider.
---@field principals? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaPrincipalList List of principals.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentAclInfoAccessRestrictionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentAclInfoAccessRestriction[]

---Unstructured data linked to this document.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentContent
---@field uri? string The URI of the content. Only Cloud Storage URIs (e.g. `gs://bucket-name/path/to/file`) are supported. The maximum file size is 2.5 MB for text-based formats, 200 MB for other formats.
---@field rawBytes? string The content represented as a stream of bytes. The maximum length is 1,000,000 bytes (1 MB / ~0.95 MiB). Note: As with all `bytes` fields, this field is represented as pure binary in Protocol Buffers and base64-encoded string in JSON. For example, `abc123!?$*&()'-=@~` should be represented as `YWJjMTIzIT8kKiYoKSctPUB+` in JSON. See https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto3#json.
---@field mimeType? string The MIME type of the content. Supported types: * `application/pdf` (PDF, only native PDFs are supported for now) * `text/html` (HTML) * `text/plain` (TXT) * `application/xml` or `text/xml` (XML) * `application/json` (JSON) * `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document` (DOCX) * `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation` (PPTX) * `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet` (XLSX) * `application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.macroenabled.12` (XLSM) The following types are supported only if layout parser is enabled in the data store: * `image/bmp` (BMP) * `image/gif` (GIF) * `image/jpeg` (JPEG) * `image/png` (PNG) * `image/tiff` (TIFF) See https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml.

---Index status of the document.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentIndexStatus
---@field pendingMessage? string Immutable. The message indicates the document index is in progress. If this field is populated, the document index is pending.
---@field errorSamples? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleRpcStatusList A sample of errors encountered while indexing the document. If this field is populated, the document is not indexed due to errors.
---@field indexTime? string The time when the document was indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours.

---Detailed document information associated with a user event.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentInfo
---@field id? string The Document resource ID.
---@field uri? string The Document URI - only allowed for website data stores.
---@field name? string The Document resource full name, of the form: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/branches/{branch_id}/documents/{document_id}`
---@field promotionIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList The promotion IDs associated with this Document. Currently, this field is restricted to at most one ID.
---@field joined? boolean Output only. Whether the referenced Document can be found in the data store.
---@field quantity? number Quantity of the Document associated with the user event. Defaults to 1. For example, this field is 2 if two quantities of the same Document are involved in a `add-to-cart` event. Required for events of the following event types: * `add-to-cart` * `purchase`
---@field conversionValue? number Optional. The conversion value associated with this Document. Must be set if UserEvent.event_type is "conversion". For example, a value of 1000 signifies that 1000 seconds were spent viewing a Document for the `watch` conversion type.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentInfoList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentInfo[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocument[]

---A singleton resource of DataStore. If it's empty when DataStore is created and DataStore is set to DataStore.ContentConfig.CONTENT_REQUIRED, the default parser will default to digital parser.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfig
---@field defaultParsingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfig Configurations for default Document parser. If not specified, we will configure it as default DigitalParsingConfig, and the default parsing config will be applied to all file types for Document parsing.
---@field name? string The full resource name of the Document Processing Config. Format: `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/dataStores/*/documentProcessingConfig`.
---@field parsingConfigOverrides? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigMap Map from file type to override the default parsing configuration based on the file type. Supported keys: * `pdf`: Override parsing config for PDF files, either digital parsing, ocr parsing or layout parsing is supported. * `html`: Override parsing config for HTML files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `docx`: Override parsing config for DOCX files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `pptx`: Override parsing config for PPTX files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `xlsm`: Override parsing config for XLSM files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `xlsx`: Override parsing config for XLSX files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported.
---@field chunkingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfig Whether chunking mode is enabled.

---Configuration for chunking config.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfig
---@field layoutBasedChunkingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfigLayoutBasedChunkingConfig Configuration for the layout based chunking.

---Configuration for the layout based chunking.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfigLayoutBasedChunkingConfig
---@field chunkSize? number The token size limit for each chunk. Supported values: 100-500 (inclusive). Default value: 500.
---@field includeAncestorHeadings? boolean Whether to include appending different levels of headings to chunks from the middle of the document to prevent context loss. Default value: False.

---Related configurations applied to a specific type of document parser.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfig
---@field digitalParsingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigDigitalParsingConfig Configurations applied to digital parser.
---@field layoutParsingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigLayoutParsingConfig Configurations applied to layout parser.
---@field ocrParsingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigOcrParsingConfig Configurations applied to OCR parser. Currently it only applies to PDFs.

---The digital parsing configurations for documents.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigDigitalParsingConfig

---The layout parsing configurations for documents.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigLayoutParsingConfig
---@field excludeHtmlClasses? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. List of HTML classes to exclude from the parsed content.
---@field excludeHtmlElements? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. List of HTML elements to exclude from the parsed content.
---@field enableImageAnnotation? boolean Optional. If true, the LLM based annotation is added to the image during parsing.
---@field enableGetProcessedDocument? boolean Optional. If true, the processed document will be made available for the GetProcessedDocument API.
---@field structuredContentTypes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. Contains the required structure types to extract from the document. Supported values: * `shareholder-structure`
---@field excludeHtmlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. List of HTML ids to exclude from the parsed content.
---@field enableTableAnnotation? boolean Optional. If true, the LLM based annotation is added to the table during parsing.
---@field enableLlmLayoutParsing? boolean Optional. If true, the pdf layout will be refined using an LLM.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfig }

---The OCR parsing configurations for documents.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigOcrParsingConfig
---@field enhancedDocumentElements? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList [DEPRECATED] This field is deprecated. To use the additional enhanced document elements processing, please switch to `layout_parsing_config`.
---@field useNativeText? boolean If true, will use native text instead of OCR text on pages containing native text.

---Double list.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDoubleList
---@field values? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.DoubleList Double values.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDoubleListMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDoubleList }

---Defines embedding config, used for bring your own embeddings feature.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEmbeddingConfig
---@field fieldPath? string Full field path in the schema mapped as embedding field.

---Request message for SiteSearchEngineService.EnableAdvancedSiteSearch method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEnableAdvancedSiteSearchRequest

---Metadata that describes the training and serving parameters of an Engine.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngine
---@field modelConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineModelConfigsValueEnumMap Optional. Maps a model name to its specific configuration for this engine. This allows admin users to turn on/off individual models. This only stores models whose states are overridden by the admin. When the state is unspecified, or model_configs is empty for this model, the system will decide if this model should be available or not based on the default configuration. For example, a preview model should be disabled by default if the admin has not chosen to enable it.
---@field sessionConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSessionConfig Optional. Non-empty default. Session config for the engine.
---@field mediaRecommendationEngineConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfig Configurations for the Media Engine. Only applicable on the data stores with solution_type SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION and IndustryVertical.MEDIA vertical.
---@field dataStoreIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. The data stores associated with this engine. For SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH and SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION type of engines, they can only associate with at most one data store. If solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT, multiple DataStores in the same Collection can be associated here. Note that when used in CreateEngineRequest, one DataStore id must be provided as the system will use it for necessary initializations.
---@field commonConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineCommonConfig Common config spec that specifies the metadata of the engine.
---@field effectiveFeatures? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnumMap Output only. The complete, server-resolved state of every known feature toggle. Unlike `features`, which stores only explicit admin overrides, this map always contains an entry for every toggle. Clients should read toggle state from this field.
---@field globalFeatureToggleState? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineGlobalFeatureToggleStateEnum Optional. Controls the global feature toggle state for the engine.
---@field marketplaceAgentVisibility? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineMarketplaceAgentVisibilityEnum Optional. The visibility of marketplace agents in the agent gallery.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability config for the engine.
---@field featurePolicies? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineFeaturePolicyMap Optional. Per-feature access policies, keyed by feature toggle name (see `features`). A feature with no entry is available to every user when it is on. Only features that support access policies are accepted.
---@field chatEngineMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineChatEngineMetadata Output only. Additional information of the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field associatedAgentRegistry? string Output only. The Agent registry containing the agents, MCP servers and tools associated with this engine. Derived server-side from the linked Agent Gateway's registry.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the engine. Should be human readable. UTF-8 encoded string with limit of 1024 characters.
---@field appType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineAppTypeEnum Optional. Immutable. This the application type which this engine resource represents. NOTE: this is a new concept independ of existing industry vertical or solution type.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was created at.
---@field connectorTenantInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringMap Optional. Maps a connector ID (e.g., "hybrid-github", "shopify") to tenant-specific information required for that connector. The structure of the tenant information string is connector-dependent.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineIndustryVerticalEnum Optional. The industry vertical that the engine registers. The restriction of the Engine industry vertical is based on DataStore: Vertical on Engine has to match vertical of the DataStore linked to the engine.
---@field knowledgeGraphConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineKnowledgeGraphConfig Optional. Configurations for the Knowledge Graph. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field disableAnalytics? boolean Optional. Whether to disable analytics for searches performed on this engine.
---@field features? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineFeaturesValueEnumMap Optional. Feature config for the engine to opt in or opt out of features. Supported keys: * `*`: all features, if it's present, all other feature state settings are ignored. * `agent-gallery` * `no-code-agent-builder` * `prompt-gallery` * `model-selector` * `notebook-lm` * `people-search` * `people-search-org-chart` * `bi-directional-audio` * `speech-to-text` * `feedback` * `session-sharing` * `personalization-memory` * `personalization-suggested-highlights` * `mobile-app-access` * `disable-agent-sharing` * `disable-image-generation` * `disable-video-generation` * `music-generation` * `speech-generation` * `disable-onedrive-upload` * `disable-talk-to-content` * `disable-google-drive-upload` * `disable-welcome-emails` * `disable-canvas` * `canvas-workspace` * `canvas-app-builder` * `skills` * `skill-sharing` * `skill-sharing-without-admin-approval` * `skill-security-scan` * `disable-projects` * `sobi` * `enable-end-user-sharing-with-groups` * `single-agent-orchestration` * `multi-agent-orchestration` * `cross-product-intelligence` * `workflow-agents` * `in-app-notifications` * `code-extraction` * `remote-vm` * `license-tier-badge` * `canvas-app-sharing` * `agent-marketplace` * `agent-scheduling` * `preview-agents` * `plugins`
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaCmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the Engine.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineSolutionTypeEnum Required. The solutions of the engine.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was last updated.
---@field procurementContactEmails? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. The emails of the procurement contacts.
---@field name? string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the engine. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}` engine should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are /a-z0-9*/. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field chatEngineConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineChatEngineConfig Configurations for the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed? boolean Output only. Whether the project is allowed to set `global_feature_toggle_state` to `DELAYED`.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach.
---@field agentGatewaySetting? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaAgentGatewaySetting Optional. The agent gateway setting for the engine.
---@field searchEngineConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineSearchEngineConfig Configurations for the Search Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineAppTypeEnum "APP_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"APP_TYPE_INTRANET"

---Configurations for a Chat Engine.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineChatEngineConfig
---@field dialogflowAgentToLink? string The resource name of an exist Dialogflow agent to link to this Chat Engine. Customers can either provide `agent_creation_config` to create agent or provide an agent name that links the agent with the Chat engine. Format: `projects//locations//agents/`. Note that the `dialogflow_agent_to_link` are one-time consumed by and passed to Dialogflow service. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation. Use ChatEngineMetadata.dialogflow_agent for actual agent association after Engine is created.
---@field agentCreationConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineChatEngineConfigAgentCreationConfig The configurationt generate the Dialogflow agent that is associated to this Engine. Note that these configurations are one-time consumed by and passed to Dialogflow service. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation.
---@field allowCrossRegion? boolean Optional. If the flag set to true, we allow the agent and engine are in different locations, otherwise the agent and engine are required to be in the same location. The flag is set to false by default. Note that the `allow_cross_region` are one-time consumed by and passed to EngineService.CreateEngine. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation.

---Configurations for generating a Dialogflow agent. Note that these configurations are one-time consumed by and passed to Dialogflow service. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineChatEngineConfigAgentCreationConfig
---@field business? string Name of the company, organization or other entity that the agent represents. Used for knowledge connector LLM prompt and for knowledge search.
---@field timeZone? string Required. The time zone of the agent from the [time zone database](https://www.iana.org/time-zones), e.g., America/New_York, Europe/Paris.
---@field location? string Agent location for Agent creation, supported values: global/us/eu. If not provided, us Engine will create Agent using us-central-1 by default; eu Engine will create Agent using eu-west-1 by default.
---@field defaultLanguageCode? string Required. The default language of the agent as a language tag. See [Language Support](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/docs/reference/language) for a list of the currently supported language codes.

---Additional information of a Chat Engine. Fields in this message are output only.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineChatEngineMetadata
---@field dialogflowAgent? string The resource name of a Dialogflow agent, that this Chat Engine refers to. Format: `projects//locations//agents/`.

---Common configurations for an Engine.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineCommonConfig
---@field companyName? string The name of the company, business or entity that is associated with the engine. Setting this may help improve LLM related features.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum "CONFIGURABLE_BILLING_APPROACH_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONFIGURABLE_BILLING_APPROACH_ENABLED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaEngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnum "FEATURE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FEATURE_STATE_ON"|"FEATURE_STATE_OFF"

