---Session specification.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchRequestSessionSpec
---@field queryId? string If set, the search result gets stored to the "turn" specified by this query ID. Example: Let's say the session looks like this: session { name: ".../sessions/xxx" turns { query { text: "What is foo?" query_id: ".../questions/yyy" } answer: "Foo is ..." } turns { query { text: "How about bar then?" query_id: ".../questions/zzz" } } } The user can call /search API with a request like this: session: ".../sessions/xxx" session_spec { query_id: ".../questions/zzz" } Then, the API stores the search result, associated with the last turn. The stored search result can be used by a subsequent /answer API call (with the session ID and the query ID specified). Also, it is possible to call /search and /answer in parallel with the same session ID & query ID.
---@field searchResultPersistenceCount? number The number of top search results to persist. The persisted search results can be used for the subsequent /answer api call. This field is similar to the `summary_result_count` field in SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.SummarySpec.summary_result_count. At most 10 results for documents mode, or 50 for chunks mode.

---The specification for query spell correction.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchRequestSpellCorrectionSpec
---@field mode? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchRequestSpellCorrectionSpecModeEnum|string The mode under which spell correction replaces the original search query. Defaults to Mode.AUTO.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchRequestSpellCorrectionSpecModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUGGESTION_ONLY"|"AUTO"

---Response message for SearchService.Search method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponse
---@field results? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultList A list of matched documents. The order represents the ranking.
---@field queryExpansionInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseQueryExpansionInfo Query expansion information for the returned results.
---@field oneBoxResults? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseOneBoxResultList A list of One Box results. There can be multiple One Box results of different types.
---@field appliedControls? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Optional. Controls applied as part of the Control service.
---@field correctedQuery? string Contains the spell corrected query, if found. If the spell correction type is AUTOMATIC, then the search results are based on corrected_query. Otherwise the original query is used for search.
---@field attributionToken? string A unique search token. This should be included in the UserEvent logs resulting from this search, which enables accurate attribution of search model performance. This also helps to identify a request during the customer support scenarios.
---@field guidedSearchResult? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResult Guided search result.
---@field sessionInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSessionInfo Session information. Only set if SearchRequest.session is provided. See its description for more details.
---@field semanticState? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSemanticStateEnum Output only. Indicates the semantic state of the search response.
---@field facets? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacetList Results of facets requested by user.
---@field summary? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummary A summary as part of the search results. This field is only returned if SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.summary_spec is set.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token that can be sent as SearchRequest.page_token to retrieve the next page. If this field is omitted, there are no subsequent pages.
---@field suggestedQuery? string Corrected query with low confidence, AKA did you mean query. Compared with corrected_query, this field is set when SpellCorrector returned a response, but FPR(full page replacement) is not triggered because the corrction is of low confidence(eg, reversed because there are matches of the original query in document corpus).
---@field geoSearchDebugInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGeoSearchDebugInfoList
---@field naturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfo Output only. Natural language query understanding information for the returned results.
---@field totalSize? number The estimated total count of matched items irrespective of pagination. The count of results returned by pagination may be less than the total_size that matches.
---@field searchLinkPromotions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchLinkPromotionList Promotions for site search.
---@field redirectUri? string The URI of a customer-defined redirect page. If redirect action is triggered, no search is performed, and only redirect_uri and attribution_token are set in the response.

---A facet result.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacet
---@field values? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacetFacetValueList The facet values for this field.
---@field key? string The key for this facet. For example, `"colors"` or `"price"`. It matches SearchRequest.FacetSpec.FacetKey.key.
---@field dynamicFacet? boolean Whether the facet is dynamically generated.

---A facet value which contains value names and their count.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacetFacetValue
---@field interval? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaInterval Interval value for a facet, such as 10, 20) for facet "price". It matches [SearchRequest.FacetSpec.FacetKey.intervals.
---@field value? string Text value of a facet, such as "Black" for facet "colors".
---@field count? string Number of items that have this facet value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacetFacetValueList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacetFacetValue[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacetList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseFacet[]

---Debug information specifically related to forward geocoding issues arising from Geolocation Search.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGeoSearchDebugInfo
---@field errorMessage? string The error produced.
---@field originalAddressQuery? string The address from which forward geocoding ingestion produced issues.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGeoSearchDebugInfoList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGeoSearchDebugInfo[]

---Guided search result. The guided search helps user to refine the search results and narrow down to the real needs from a broaded search results.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResult
---@field refinementAttributes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResultRefinementAttributeList A list of ranked refinement attributes.
---@field followUpQuestions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Suggested follow-up questions.

---Useful attribute for search result refinements.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResultRefinementAttribute
---@field attributeValue? string Attribute value used to refine the results. For example, `"drama"`.
---@field attributeKey? string Attribute key used to refine the results. For example, `"movie_type"`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResultRefinementAttributeList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResultRefinementAttribute[]

---Information describing what natural language understanding was done on the input query.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfo
---@field classifiedIntents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList The classified intents from the input query.
---@field extractedFilters? string The filters that were extracted from the input query.
---@field structuredExtractedFilter? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilter The filters that were extracted from the input query represented in a structured form.
---@field rewrittenQuery? string Rewritten input query minus the extracted filters.

---The filters that were extracted from the input query represented in a structured form.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilter
---@field expression? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterExpression The expression denoting the filter that was extracted from the input query in a structured form. It can be a simple expression denoting a single string, numerical or geolocation constraint or a compound expression which is a combination of multiple expressions connected using logical (OR and AND) operators.

---Logical `And` operator.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterAndExpression
---@field expressions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterExpressionList The expressions that were ANDed together.

---The expression denoting the filter that was extracted from the input query.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterExpression
---@field numberConstraint? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterNumberConstraint Numerical constraint expression.
---@field orExpr? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterOrExpression Logical "Or" compound operator connecting multiple expressions.
---@field stringConstraint? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterStringConstraint String constraint expression.
---@field geolocationConstraint? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterGeolocationConstraint Geolocation constraint expression.
---@field andExpr? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterAndExpression Logical "And" compound operator connecting multiple expressions.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterExpressionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterExpression[]

---Constraint of a geolocation field. Name of the geolocation field as defined in the schema.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterGeolocationConstraint
---@field longitude? number The longitude of the geolocation inferred from the input query.
---@field fieldName? string The name of the geolocation field as defined in the schema.
---@field radiusInMeters? number The radius in meters around the address. The record is returned if the location of the geolocation field is within the radius.
---@field address? string The reference address that was inferred from the input query. The proximity of the reference address to the geolocation field will be used to filter the results.
---@field latitude? number The latitude of the geolocation inferred from the input query.

---Constraint expression of a number field. Example: price < 100.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterNumberConstraint
---@field fieldName? string Name of the numerical field as defined in the schema.
---@field comparison? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterNumberConstraintComparisonEnum The comparison operation performed between the field value and the value specified in the constraint.
---@field value? number The value specified in the numerical constraint.
---@field querySegment? string Identifies the keywords within the search query that match a filter.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterNumberConstraintComparisonEnum "COMPARISON_UNSPECIFIED"|"EQUALS"|"LESS_THAN_EQUALS"|"LESS_THAN"|"GREATER_THAN_EQUALS"|"GREATER_THAN"

---Logical `Or` operator.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterOrExpression
---@field expressions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterExpressionList The expressions that were ORed together.

---Constraint expression of a string field.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfoStructuredExtractedFilterStringConstraint
---@field querySegment? string Identifies the keywords within the search query that match a filter.
---@field fieldName? string Name of the string field as defined in the schema.
---@field values? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.StringList Values of the string field. The record will only be returned if the field value matches one of the values specified here.

---OneBoxResult is a holder for all results of specific type that we want to display in UI differently.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseOneBoxResult
---@field oneBoxType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseOneBoxResultOneBoxTypeEnum The type of One Box result.
---@field searchResults? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultList The search results for this One Box.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseOneBoxResultList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseOneBoxResult[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseOneBoxResultOneBoxTypeEnum "ONE_BOX_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PEOPLE"|"ORGANIZATION"|"SLACK"|"KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH"

---Information describing query expansion including whether expansion has occurred.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseQueryExpansionInfo
---@field pinnedResultCount? string Number of pinned results. This field will only be set when expansion happens and SearchRequest.QueryExpansionSpec.pin_unexpanded_results is set to true.
---@field expandedQuery? boolean Bool describing whether query expansion has occurred.

---Represents the search results.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResult
---@field rankSignals? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRankSignals Optional. A set of ranking signals associated with the result.
---@field document? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDocument The document data snippet in the search response. Only fields that are marked as `retrievable` are populated.
---@field retrievalSignals? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRetrievalSignals Optional. A set of signals used by the relevance filter meant for use to fine-tune the relevance filter thresholds.
---@field id? string Document.id of the searched Document.
---@field chunk? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaChunk The chunk data in the search response if the SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.search_result_mode is set to CHUNKS.
---@field modelScores? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDoubleListMap Output only. Google provided available scores.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResult[]

---A set of ranking signals.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRankSignals
---@field customSignals? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRankSignalsCustomSignalList Optional. A list of custom clearbox signals.
---@field relevanceScore? number Optional. Semantic relevance adjustment.
---@field semanticSimilarityScore? number Optional. Semantic similarity adjustment.
---@field pctrRank? number Optional. Predicted conversion rate adjustment as a rank.
---@field documentAge? number Optional. Age of the document in hours.
---@field precomputedExpressionValues? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.DoubleList Optional. A list of precomputed expression results for a given document, in the same order as requested in `SearchRequest.custom_ranking_params.expressions_to_precompute`.
---@field defaultRank? number Optional. The default rank of the result.
---@field boostingFactor? number Optional. Combined custom boosts for a doc.
---@field topicalityRank? number Optional. Topicality adjustment as a rank.
---@field keywordSimilarityScore? number Optional. Keyword matching adjustment.

---Custom clearbox signal represented by name and value pair.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRankSignalsCustomSignal
---@field name? string Optional. Name of the signal.
---@field value? number Optional. Float value representing the ranking signal (e.g. 1.25 for BM25).

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRankSignalsCustomSignalList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRankSignalsCustomSignal[]

---Contains a set of signals used by the relevance filter.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRetrievalSignals
---@field retrievalSources? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRetrievalSignalsRetrievalSourcesItemEnumList Optional. Indicates how the result was retrieved.
---@field semanticRelevanceScore? number Optional. Relevance score used by the filter when semantic_relevance_threshold is set.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRetrievalSignalsRetrievalSourcesItemEnum "RETRIEVAL_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"KEYWORD_SEARCH"|"SEMANTIC_SEARCH"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRetrievalSignalsRetrievalSourcesItemEnumList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSearchResultRetrievalSignalsRetrievalSourcesItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSemanticStateEnum "SEMANTIC_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DISABLED"|"ENABLED"

---Information about the session.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSessionInfo
---@field queryId? string Query ID that corresponds to this search API call. One session can have multiple turns, each with a unique query ID. By specifying the session name and this query ID in the Answer API call, the answer generation happens in the context of the search results from this search call.
---@field name? string Name of the session. If the auto-session mode is used (when SearchRequest.session ends with "-"), this field holds the newly generated session name.

---Summary of the top N search results specified by the summary spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummary
---@field summaryText? string The summary content.
---@field safetyAttributes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummarySafetyAttributes A collection of Safety Attribute categories and their associated confidence scores.
---@field summaryWithMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummarySummaryWithMetadata Summary with metadata information.
---@field summarySkippedReasons? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummarySummarySkippedReasonsItemEnumList Additional summary-skipped reasons. This provides the reason for ignored cases. If nothing is skipped, this field is not set.

---Stores binarydata attached to text answer, e.g. image, video, audio, etc.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachment
---@field attributionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachmentAttributionTypeEnum|string Output only. The attribution type of the blob.
---@field data? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachmentBlob Output only. The blob data.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachmentAttributionTypeEnum "ATTRIBUTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CORPUS"|"GENERATED"

---Stores type and data of the blob.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachmentBlob
---@field mimeType? string Output only. The media type (MIME type) of the generated data.
---@field data? string Output only. Raw bytes.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachmentList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryBlobAttachment[]

---Citation info for a segment.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitation
---@field startIndex? string Index indicates the start of the segment, measured in bytes/unicode.
---@field endIndex? string End of the attributed segment, exclusive.
---@field sources? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationSourceList Citation sources for the attributed segment.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitation[]

---Citation metadata.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationMetadata
---@field citations? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationList Citations for segments.

---Citation source.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationSource
---@field referenceIndex? string Document reference index from SummaryWithMetadata.references. It is 0-indexed and the value will be zero if the reference_index is not set explicitly.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationSourceList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryCitationSource[]

---Document reference.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryReference
---@field document? string Required. Document.name of the document. Full resource name of the referenced document, in the format `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/dataStores/*/branches/*/documents/*`.
---@field title? string Title of the document.
---@field chunkContents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryReferenceChunkContentList List of cited chunk contents derived from document content.
---@field uri? string Cloud Storage or HTTP uri for the document.

---Chunk content.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1beta.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaSearchResponseSummaryReferenceChunkContent
